2 Sam. 24:5).","verses":6,"v":[8]},{"id":"baal-meon_144","name":"Baal-meon","kind":"City","lat":31.67945,"lon":35.73489,"summary":"Lord of dwelling, a town of Reuben (Num. 32:38), called also Beth-meon (Jer. 48:23) and Beth-baal-meon (Josh. 13:17). It is supposed to have been the birth-place of Elisha.","verses":3,"v":[8]},{"id":"nebo_883","name":"Nebo","kind":"Church","lat":31.76772,"lon":35.72618,"summary":"A Chaldean god whose worship was introduced into Assyria by Pul (Isa. 46:1; Jer. 48:1). To this idol was dedicated the great temple whose ruins are still seen at Birs Nimrud.","verses":7,"v":[8]},{"id":"euphrates_421","name":"Euphrates","kind":"Water (River)","lat":34.74942,"lon":40.9364,"summary":"Hebrew, Perath; Assyrian, Purat; Persian cuneiform, Ufratush, whence Greek Euphrates, meaning “sweet water.” The Assyrian name means “the stream,” or “the great stream.”","verses":32,"v":[9]},{"id":"gilead_475","name":"Gilead","kind":"Region","lat":32.75,"lon":35.75,"summary":"Hill of testimony, (Gen. 31:21), a mountainous region east of Jordan. From its mountainous character it is called “the mount of Gilead” (Gen. 31:25).","verses":80,"v":[9,10,16]},{"id":"bashan_159","name":"Bashan","kind":"Region","lat":32.80008,"lon":35.9373,"summary":"Light soil, first mentioned in Gen. 14:5, where it is said that Chedorlaomer and his confederates “smote the Rephaim in Ashteroth,” where Og the king of Bashan had his residence.","verses":52,"v":[11,12,16,23]},{"id":"gad_1286","name":"Gad","kind":"Region","lat":32.04697,"lon":35.7458,"summary":"Added from Digital Manna places-1262 (LPF sync 2026-10-13)","verses":21,"v":[11]},{"id":"salecah_1017","name":"Salecah","kind":"City","lat":32.49394,"lon":36.71034,"summary":"Wandering, a city of Bashan assigned to the half tribe of Manasseh (Deut. 3:10; Josh. 12:5; 13:11), identified with Salkhad, about 56 miles east of Jordan.","verses":4,"v":[11]},{"id":"sharon_1064","name":"Sharon","kind":"","lat":33.41616,"lon":35.85726,"summary":"","verses":1,"v":[16]},{"id":"east-manasseh-half-tribe_1290","name":"East Manasseh (Half-Tribe)","kind":"Region","lat":32.64111,"lon":36.07154,"summary":"Added from Digital Manna places-1268 (LPF sync 2026-10-13)","verses":14,"v":[18,23,26]},{"id":"jetur_641","name":"Jetur","kind":"","lat":33.41616,"lon":35.85726,"summary":"An enclosure, one of the twelve sons of Ishmael (Gen. 25:15).","verses":1,"v":[19]},{"id":"naphish_876","name":"Naphish","kind":"","lat":32.80008,"lon":35.9373,"summary":"Refresher, one of the sons of Ishmael (Gen. 25:15; 1 Chr. 1:31).","verses":1,"v":[19]},{"id":"nodab_903","name":"Nodab","kind":"","lat":32.80008,"lon":35.9373,"summary":"Noble, probably a tribe descended from one of the sons of Ishmael, with whom the trans-Jordanic tribes made war (1 Chr. 5:19).","verses":1,"v":[19]},{"id":"baal-hermon_143","name":"Baal-hermon","kind":"City","lat":33.41616,"lon":35.85726,"summary":"A city near Mount Hermon inhabited by the Ephraimites (1 Chr. 5:23).","verses":1,"v":[23]},{"id":"mount_hermon_841","name":"mount Hermon","kind":"Mountain","lat":33.41611,"lon":35.8575,"summary":"","verses":7,"v":[23]},{"id":"senir_1047","name":"Senir","kind":"","lat":33.41616,"lon":35.85726,"summary":"Shenir, the name given to Hermon by the Amorites (Deut. 3:9). It means “coat of mail” or “breastplate,” and is equivalent to “Sirion.” Some interpret the word as meaning “the prominent” or “the snowy mountain.”","verses":4,"v":[23]},{"id":"gozan_492","name":"Gozan","kind":"Region","lat":36.84001,"lon":40.06889,"summary":"A region in Central Asia to which the Israelites were carried away captive (2 Kings 17:6; 1 Chr. 5:26; 2 Kings 19:12; Isa. 37:12). It was situated in Mesopotamia, on the river Habor (2 Kings 17:6; 18:11), the Khabur, a tributary of the Euphrates.","verses":5,"v":[26]},{"id":"habor_499","name":"Habor","kind":"Water (River)","lat":36.34497,"lon":40.78933,"summary":"The united stream, or, according to others, with beautiful banks, the name of a river in Assyria, and also of the district through which it flowed (1 Chr. 5:26).","verses":3,"v":[26]},{"id":"halah_508","name":"Halah","kind":"Region","lat":36.34497,"lon":40.78933,"summary":"A district of Media to which captive Israelites were transported by the Assyrian kings (2 Kings 17:6; 18:11; 1 Chr. 5:26). It lay along the banks of the upper Khabur, from its source to its junction with the Jerujer.","verses":3,"v":[26]},{"id":"hara_525","name":"Hara","kind":"Region","lat":36.34497,"lon":40.78933,"summary":"Mountainous land, a province of Assyria (1 Chr. 5:26), between the Tigris and the Euphrates, along the banks of the Khabur, to which some of the Israelite captives were carried.","verses":1,"v":[26]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[1121,1121,1121,1121,7205,7205,1060,1060,3478,3478,1931,1931,1060,1060,1060,1062,1062,5414,5414,1121,1121,1121,3130,3130,1121,3478,3478,2490,2490,2490,1,1,3326,3808,3808,3808,3808,3187,1062,1062,1062],[3588,3588,3063,1396,251,251,251,5057,5057,5057,4480,4480,4480,1062,1062,3130,3130,3130],[1121,1121,7205,7205,1060,1060,3478,3478,2585,6396,2696,3756,3756],[1121,1121,3100,3100,8098,1121,1121,1463,1121,1121,8096,1121,1121],[4318,1121,1121,7211,1121,1121,1168,1121,1121],[880,880,1121,1121,834,8407,4428,804,804,1540,1540,1540,1931,5387,5387,5387,7206,7206,7206],[251,251,4940,4940,4940,3187,3187,8435,8435,8435,3273,7218,7218,2148],[1106,1106,1121,5811,5811,1121,1121,8087,8087,1121,1121,3100,3100,1931,3427,6177,6177,5704,5704,5704,5704,5015,1186,1186],[3427,3427,3427,4217,4217,4217,5704,5704,5704,4057,4057,4057,4057,4057,4480,4480,6578,6578,6578,5104,3588,4735,4735,7235,7235,776,776,776,1568,1568],[3117,3117,3117,7586,7586,6213,6213,4421,5973,1905,1905,5307,5307,5307,3027,3027,3027,3427,3427,3427,168,168,168,168,168,5921,6440,6440,4217,1568,1568],[1121,1121,1410,1410,3427,5048,5048,5048,5048,776,776,776,1316,1316,5704,5548,5548,5548],[3100,3100,7218,7218,8223,4932,4932,3285,3285,8202,8202,1316,1316,1316